  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The study focuses exclusively on the five largest collective accommodation centers, which may not represent the dynamics of the wider, more dispersed network of smaller centers across Poland.",
      "what": "This study evaluated the urban integration of collective accommodation centers (CACs) for Ukrainian refugees in Poland using an experimental, three-phase research framework that combined artificial intelligence with GIS environments. Focusing on the five largest CACs, the analysis assessed their integration into the surrounding neighborhoods against the principles of the 15-minute city and documented local integration initiatives.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that while local integration events occurred, they lacked permanence, meaning these accommodation centers missed the opportunity to leave a lasting, positive physical or social imprint on the surrounding urban landscape."
